WEBVTT

00:00.554 --> 00:03.943
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:03.987 --> 00:07.258
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:07.293 --> 00:10.829
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.865 --> 00:13.835
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.870 --> 00:17.341
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.377 --> 00:20.648
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.683 --> 00:22.283
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.318 --> 00:23.586
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.621 --> 00:29.229
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.778 --> 00:38.545
Ugh. This is gonna suck.

00:38.580 --> 00:40.649
80% of these acts are either air guitar

00:40.685 --> 00:42.752
<i>or girls dancing to songs from Frozen.</i>

00:42.788 --> 00:45.358
Yeah, back in my day you
had to be a triple threat

00:45.393 --> 00:46.759
to even get on that stage.

00:46.795 --> 00:48.128
You were a triple threat?

00:48.164 --> 00:49.165
I sure was.

00:49.200 --> 00:50.499
I could sing, dance,

00:50.535 --> 00:53.439
and guess the weight of any
baby that was tossed to me.

00:54.809 --> 00:57.412
♪ I'm a Yankee Doodle Dandy ♪

00:57.448 --> 00:58.413
Eight pounds!

00:58.449 --> 01:00.684
♪ Yankee Doodle do or die ♪

01:00.720 --> 01:01.886
12-nine! A big one!

01:01.922 --> 01:05.192
♪ A real live nephew of my Uncle Sam ♪

01:05.227 --> 01:07.730
♪ Born on the Fourth of July ♪

01:07.765 --> 01:10.435
Three pounds? Someone
couldn't wait to be here.

01:20.254 --> 01:21.421
Did that really happen?

01:21.456 --> 01:24.126
Nah, I just lip-synced "Born to Run."

01:24.161 --> 01:25.695
The show is about to start.

01:25.730 --> 01:27.465
I-Is Daddy still parking the car?

01:27.501 --> 01:29.902
Yes. Everything takes
him longer these days.

01:29.937 --> 01:32.340
His cataracts are getting worse.

01:32.375 --> 01:35.079
Hey, Lois, look over there...
It's Jessica Chastain.

01:35.114 --> 01:37.449
Oh, Daddy, that's Bryce Dallas Howard.

01:37.484 --> 01:39.586
You're blind as a bat.

01:52.478 --> 01:56.049
Okay, for the first of our
65 performances tonight...

01:56.084 --> 01:58.219
- You got to be kidding!
- Son of a bitch!

01:58.254 --> 02:00.857
I agree. Now please welcome Meg Griffin

02:00.892 --> 02:03.462
and Ruth Cochammer. No laughing.

02:03.497 --> 02:05.064
It's "Coke-a-mer"!

02:05.099 --> 02:06.868
Not in the boys' room it isn't.

02:11.744 --> 02:14.214
♪ One, two, three and to the four ♪

02:14.249 --> 02:16.885
♪ Meg Meggy Meg and Dr.
Ruth is at the door... ♪

02:16.920 --> 02:19.490
Wake up, people, Monsanto
is poisoning the world

02:19.525 --> 02:21.827
with frankenfoods, and
we're letting it happen.

02:21.863 --> 02:23.931
Monsanto equals murder!

02:23.967 --> 02:26.101
- Monsanto equals murder!
- That's enough.

02:26.136 --> 02:28.639
I am so sick of this
being used as a platform

02:28.674 --> 02:30.978
to attack genetically modified foods.

02:31.013 --> 02:33.013
You can't silence the truth!

02:33.048 --> 02:34.350
What, what?

02:34.385 --> 02:35.752
It's over, Patty.

02:35.787 --> 02:38.123
Hi, Patty. I like Patty.

02:40.829 --> 02:43.633
Okay, up next, here's Evelyn Fong,

02:43.668 --> 02:45.936
our 11-year-old high school junior.

03:03.236 --> 03:05.337
Oh, my God.

03:05.372 --> 03:06.906
What is that?

03:06.942 --> 03:10.212
It's... it's the most beautiful
thing I've ever heard.

03:10.248 --> 03:12.116
It's a violin, Peter.

03:12.152 --> 03:14.620
And now, two football players
are going to do something

03:14.655 --> 03:17.492
that only makes sense to the
rest of the football team.

03:17.528 --> 03:19.194
Coach, the bus is here.

03:19.229 --> 03:21.232
This is an away game?

03:21.268 --> 03:23.436
It's true!

03:23.471 --> 03:25.073
Remember that happened?

03:25.108 --> 03:27.543
Those are the
kids I bought beer for.

03:27.578 --> 03:30.047
- I got to take a leak.
- Daddy, you can't see.

03:30.083 --> 03:31.950
Let me help you to the bathroom.

03:31.986 --> 03:33.420
I can see fine.

03:34.191 --> 03:36.726
All right, there's only
so many seats on the bus.

03:36.761 --> 03:39.230
One of you will have to sit next to me.

03:39.265 --> 03:40.799
I will, Coach.

03:42.138 --> 03:44.573
Oh! He talked
on the whole bus ride!

03:47.880 --> 03:49.583
How are you, gentlemen

03:49.618 --> 03:51.084
Dude! What the hell?

03:51.120 --> 03:52.920
Whoa! With cataracts like those,

03:52.956 --> 03:55.159
<i>someone needs a big pair of glasses.</i>

03:55.194 --> 03:57.046
Hey! Jessica Chastain!

04:01.805 --> 04:03.774
I'm glad you finally agreed to have

04:03.809 --> 04:05.443
the cataract surgery, Daddy.

04:05.478 --> 04:06.646
I wish I hadn't!

04:06.682 --> 04:08.782
I can't see anything
now! This is terrible!

04:08.817 --> 04:12.488
Well, tha-that's why the whole
family came to support you.

04:12.524 --> 04:15.528
Oh, really? Oh, wow, that's
so kind. Who's here?

04:15.563 --> 04:17.933
Oh, uh, well, as you know, I'm here.

04:17.967 --> 04:20.961
- Who else?
- Uh, Stewie and Brian.

04:20.994 --> 04:22.573
Hey, hope you feel better soon.

04:22.608 --> 04:24.711
That doesn't sound
like the whole family.

04:24.746 --> 04:27.583
Hey, hope those
eyes get better soon, Pop.

04:27.618 --> 04:29.819
It's me, Peter. Shipoopi.

04:29.854 --> 04:31.824
Oh, thanks for coming, Peter.

04:31.859 --> 04:34.186
I-I'm here, too, Grandpa.

04:34.240 --> 04:38.167
And, uh, and Meg went down
to-to put money in the meter.

04:38.203 --> 04:39.470
Aw, I don't care.

04:39.505 --> 04:41.674
Now, Mr. Pewterschmidt, your
vision will be impaired

04:41.709 --> 04:43.677
for a few weeks while you recover.

04:43.712 --> 04:45.748
I recommend you and your
wife have someone around

04:45.783 --> 04:47.217
to help you during this time.

04:47.252 --> 04:49.187
Well, I'd love to help you, Daddy,

04:49.223 --> 04:51.357
but Stewie's just been so fussy lately.

04:51.392 --> 04:54.362
He's constantly crying for no reason.

04:54.398 --> 04:55.665
What are you talking about? I'm fine.

04:55.701 --> 04:57.068
Ow! Bitch!

04:57.103 --> 04:58.503
She does this a lot!

04:58.538 --> 05:00.507
You know, maybe Brian could help you.

05:00.542 --> 05:02.944
He could be your service dog.

05:02.981 --> 05:04.890
Come on, Lois,
I don't want to do that.

05:04.991 --> 05:06.785
Your father and I have
nothing in common.

05:06.820 --> 05:08.988
Brian, please. If you do this for me,

05:09.023 --> 05:11.125
you'll be a hero... just like King Arthur

05:11.161 --> 05:13.564
when he pulled the sword from the stone.

05:15.669 --> 05:18.205
Oh... yeah!

05:18.240 --> 05:19.406
Whew!

05:19.442 --> 05:21.143
Oh, God, this is embarrassing.

05:21.179 --> 05:23.046
I'm so sorry.

05:23.081 --> 05:24.950
It's been, like, 500 years.

05:24.985 --> 05:28.523
Aw, this is your big
moment and I'm ruining it.

05:34.101 --> 05:35.937
Peter, what the hell are you doing?

05:35.972 --> 05:38.440
I'm learning violin. It's
kind of like my new hobby.

05:38.475 --> 05:41.046
Well, if we're talking
about new hobbies...

05:42.249 --> 05:44.184
What is this? It's a Mason jar

05:44.220 --> 05:45.787
filled with layered sand.

05:45.822 --> 05:47.590
You can put it in your bathroom

05:47.625 --> 05:49.627
or anywhere you want to feel peaceful.

05:50.630 --> 05:52.031
Now it's nothing.

05:52.067 --> 05:53.801
I always liked the violin,

05:53.836 --> 05:56.395
'cause it kind of has
curves like a lady.

05:56.426 --> 05:58.910
Hey, you know what? Maybe you guys
can learn an instrument, too,

05:58.945 --> 06:00.614
and then we could all play together.

06:00.649 --> 06:02.350
Really? That sounds like a lot of work.

06:02.385 --> 06:04.821
Yeah, no offense, muchacho,
but I don't know

06:04.856 --> 06:07.024
if I have time for that, muchacho.

06:07.059 --> 06:08.460
Yeah, you're doing "muchacho" wrong.

06:08.495 --> 06:10.330
Come on, guys, it could be cool.

06:10.366 --> 06:12.333
I did play the oboe in high school,

06:12.369 --> 06:14.437
and the girls wouldn't leave me alone.

06:14.473 --> 06:16.307
Girls do like guys in a band.

06:16.343 --> 06:17.510
I'm in. Giggity.

06:17.545 --> 06:20.782
Oh, Quagmire,
you are so predictable.

06:20.817 --> 06:22.919
And that's why I love you, muchacho.

06:22.954 --> 06:24.789
See? That's how you do "muchacho."

06:24.824 --> 06:26.625
And, you know, there's four of us...

06:26.661 --> 06:28.295
We could be a string quartet.

06:28.330 --> 06:29.564
All right, I'll do it.

06:29.600 --> 06:32.101
But first you guys got
to do one thing for me.

06:32.137 --> 06:33.404
Sure, Joe. What is it?

06:33.439 --> 06:35.107
I want you to put me in the booth.

06:35.143 --> 06:37.512
I want to feel like a
person for a second.

06:37.547 --> 06:38.847
Aw, yeah, sure, no problem.

06:38.883 --> 06:41.051
All right, Quagmire, you
do upper, I'll do lower?

06:41.086 --> 06:42.287
Sure. Let's do it!

06:51.973 --> 06:54.039
Wow. Thanks, guys.

06:55.079 --> 06:57.079
Uh-oh.

06:57.114 --> 06:59.351
Hey, guys, guys, put him back up.

06:59.386 --> 07:00.504
I just thought of something.

07:05.997 --> 07:07.877
This is gonna be a blast.

07:14.370 --> 07:17.508
Mr. Pewterschmidt, your
service dog has arrived.

07:17.578 --> 07:19.279
- Hey, Carter.
- Brian!

07:19.315 --> 07:21.650
Y-You have a butler? Then why am I here?

07:21.685 --> 07:23.688
<i>- Why can't he help you?
- What? That's stupid.</i>

07:23.724 --> 07:24.780
Who would announce him?

07:24.827 --> 07:26.126
See, this right here,

07:26.162 --> 07:28.298
this is the one-percenter
crap I can't stand.

07:28.334 --> 07:30.869
Yes, it is. Now, sit your
99-percenter ass down

07:30.904 --> 07:32.506
and read me the comics.

07:33.776 --> 07:36.613
Okay. The Wizard of Id is
addressing his subjects.

07:36.648 --> 07:38.649
- Is he up on that balcony?
- Yes.

07:38.684 --> 07:40.686
Ha-ha! Then it's a good one.

07:50.205 --> 07:52.007
Okay, hang on, hang on, hang on.

07:52.042 --> 07:53.576
Peter, what note are you playing?

07:53.611 --> 07:55.779
I-I'm sorry, I'm not familiar. Note?

07:55.815 --> 07:57.383
Haven't you been practicing?

07:57.418 --> 07:58.852
All right, fine, I haven't.

07:58.887 --> 08:00.821
But I've been doing other violin stuff.

08:00.857 --> 08:03.326
Like I bought this jacket
like what Bugs Bunny wears

08:03.361 --> 08:05.362
when he's with that opera guy.

08:06.367 --> 08:07.934
Wow, that looks sharp.

08:07.969 --> 08:11.206
Yeah, I've been practicing
how to sit down in it.

08:11.242 --> 08:13.979
Ew, Peter, those tails are soaking wet.

08:14.014 --> 08:16.349
They may have been in the toilet.

08:20.391 --> 08:21.959
Brian! Get in here!

08:21.994 --> 08:23.529
Wh-What's up? What do you need?

08:23.564 --> 08:25.432
I'm done with my bath.
Put on this lady wig

08:25.467 --> 08:28.537
- and help me out of the tub.
- What? Why do I have to wear a wig?

08:28.572 --> 08:30.341
Otherwise it's weird.

08:31.778 --> 08:33.245
Thank you, Penelope.

08:33.281 --> 08:35.617
Hey, it's 4:30... time for dinner.

08:35.652 --> 08:38.955
But first, grab that Gold
Bond and powder my speed bag.

08:43.231 --> 08:45.491
Ah. There's the tingle.

08:52.688 --> 08:55.324
Wow, so you can just
bypass all that gridlock?

08:55.369 --> 08:56.854
Having a helicopter's amazing!

08:56.889 --> 08:58.958
And that's not all... I also use it

08:58.993 --> 09:01.294
to throw boxes of frogs
down on that church.

09:01.330 --> 09:03.065
They go bananas!

09:03.100 --> 09:06.738
Boy, I could really get used
to this rich guy stuff.

09:52.554 --> 09:53.920
You guys, I got great news!

09:53.956 --> 09:56.059
Some skank I used to
bang is getting married,

09:56.094 --> 09:58.161
and they need someone to
play at the ceremony.

09:58.196 --> 10:01.033
- We got our first gig!
- Wow, a wedding... that's awesome!

10:01.069 --> 10:03.036
All right, then we should
probably practice our piece.

10:13.985 --> 10:16.455
Wait, hold on, hold on.
Peter, uh, that's terrible.

10:16.489 --> 10:18.756
You sounded like you
were strangling a cat.

10:18.791 --> 10:21.161
Well, I was... that's how I
got revved up to perform.

10:21.221 --> 10:22.787
No, just now. Look, it's clear

10:22.822 --> 10:24.658
that you still haven't practiced at all.

10:24.694 --> 10:26.762
Yeah, this was your idea
in the first place,

10:26.797 --> 10:28.932
but you're the only one
who's done no work.

10:28.968 --> 10:31.703
No work? I stared in a mirror for hours

10:31.738 --> 10:34.709
playing air violin to the
song "Bittersweet Symphony."

10:34.744 --> 10:36.545
Peter, you're out of the group.

10:36.580 --> 10:37.681
What?!

10:37.717 --> 10:40.585
Well, fine. Screw you guys!

10:41.757 --> 10:43.690
Wow, he seemed pretty angry.

10:43.726 --> 10:45.328
Yeah, I haven't seen him this upset

10:45.364 --> 10:47.999
since he got caught using that fake ID.

10:48.034 --> 10:50.047
Can I see your ID, please?

10:53.578 --> 10:55.379
Give me one second.

10:55.414 --> 10:58.705
Uh, sir, that lady who came in
and ate all the pies is back.

11:03.295 --> 11:05.730
Okay, let's see how
those eyes are doing.

11:05.766 --> 11:07.834
See if you can tell me where Waldo is.

11:07.869 --> 11:10.071
He's right there buying
an ice cream cone.

11:10.106 --> 11:12.409
Damn it! I've been stuck
on that page for two days.

11:12.444 --> 11:14.178
Oh, and your eyes are fine.

11:14.214 --> 11:15.878
Hey, that's terrific, Carter!

11:15.912 --> 11:17.116
Seems like it's time to go home

11:17.152 --> 11:19.354
and pour some of that Scotch
of yours to celebrate.

11:19.389 --> 11:21.123
That sounds like a great idea.

11:21.159 --> 11:22.559
See you later. Wait, wait, wait.

11:22.595 --> 11:23.796
What are you talking about?

11:23.831 --> 11:25.297
I meant, like... like, both of us.

11:25.333 --> 11:26.767
Didn't you hear him? I'm all healed.

11:26.803 --> 11:28.537
I don't need a service dog anymore.

11:28.572 --> 11:30.040
What are you saying?

11:30.076 --> 11:31.443
I'm saying I'm done with you.

11:31.478 --> 11:32.744
Now, before I go,

11:32.779 --> 11:37.386
I'm just gonna old-man
drink this glass of water.

11:47.138 --> 11:49.240
Now, to take an old man pee.

11:51.446 --> 11:53.814
Ow. Ow.

11:53.850 --> 11:55.385
Ow.

11:55.420 --> 11:58.456
Ow. Ow.

11:58.492 --> 11:59.959
Ow.

11:59.994 --> 12:02.630
Ow. Ow.

12:02.667 --> 12:04.033
Ow.

12:04.068 --> 12:06.671
Ow. Ow.

12:06.706 --> 12:09.543
Ow. Ow.

12:10.330 --> 12:12.065
Ow.

12:16.964 --> 12:19.050
Oh, Brian, just in time for dinner.

12:19.089 --> 12:20.624
We're having sloppy Joes.

12:20.640 --> 12:21.941
Eh, what else you got?

12:21.968 --> 12:23.736
How about a knuckle sandwich?

12:23.772 --> 12:25.505
If Peter said that,

12:25.540 --> 12:27.777
you all would've lost
your minds laughing.

12:27.812 --> 12:29.178
It's just that at Carter's house,

12:29.213 --> 12:30.515
if you don't want something heavy,

12:30.550 --> 12:32.785
├Йtienne will whip you up an
egg dish with some shallots

12:32.820 --> 12:34.722
and chanterelles or whatever's fresh.

12:34.757 --> 12:36.558
Yeah, I know all about ├Йtienne.

12:36.593 --> 12:38.963
He climbed into my bed when I was 11.

12:40.200 --> 12:42.201
I'm sure this is a step
down for you, Bri,

12:42.236 --> 12:43.838
but now you're back in the real world

12:43.873 --> 12:45.941
where our poop stinks,
and we all eat garbage.

12:45.977 --> 12:47.143
Yeah, I guess I got used

12:47.179 --> 12:49.014
to being a little pampered
over at Carter's.

12:49.049 --> 12:50.916
Well, I'd be careful
with your uptown ways.

12:50.951 --> 12:52.921
Some of the other kids don't like it.

12:54.759 --> 12:56.494
He thinks he's better than us.

12:56.529 --> 12:58.664
What time you going to bed, fancy boy?

12:58.699 --> 13:00.267
I don't know. 9:00?

13:00.303 --> 13:01.803
9:00, Chris.

13:01.839 --> 13:04.273
Look, it's not even about the stuff.

13:04.309 --> 13:06.378
Carter and I became friends.

13:06.413 --> 13:07.947
Wait a minute! Of course!

13:07.982 --> 13:10.418
Whatever you're going to say
next, I bet it's wrong.

13:10.453 --> 13:13.190
I offended Carter by
offering to work for him.

13:13.226 --> 13:14.959
I mean, once it became a friendship,

13:14.994 --> 13:16.830
he didn't want me working for him.

13:16.866 --> 13:18.098
He wanted a pal.

13:18.134 --> 13:19.367
Brian, you're not kidding anyone.

13:19.403 --> 13:21.238
We all know you don't care about Carter.

13:21.273 --> 13:22.639
You only care about his money.

13:22.674 --> 13:24.676
<i>No, no, no. He knows I'm his friend.</i>

13:24.712 --> 13:27.848
Yeah, right. That's what Woody
thought about Buzz Lightyear.

13:27.884 --> 13:30.421
Bo Peep!

13:30.456 --> 13:32.723
What-what's going on here?

13:32.758 --> 13:36.217
Um... you've got a friend in me?

13:40.673 --> 13:42.408
What are you doing here?

13:42.444 --> 13:44.545
I-I thought you were
rehearsing with the guys.

13:44.580 --> 13:47.116
Ah, the bastards kicked me out
'cause I'm not good enough.

13:47.151 --> 13:48.718
Oh, and they also taught me

13:48.754 --> 13:52.288
that if your hand is bigger than
your face, you have cancer,

13:52.865 --> 13:56.532
so maybe you should, uh,
you know, do the test.

13:56.568 --> 13:58.737
<i>I had cancer, Peter. Remember?</i>

13:58.773 --> 14:01.173
I was in the hospital? You
weren't there for it.

14:01.209 --> 14:02.878
Well, maybe you have it again.

14:02.913 --> 14:04.813
Peter, I'm not falling for your trick,

14:04.849 --> 14:06.517
but if you're upset about the guys

14:06.553 --> 14:08.855
kicking you out of the group,
you can't really blame them.

14:08.890 --> 14:11.793
The violin takes
discipline and dedication.

14:11.828 --> 14:13.696
You never even practiced.

14:13.731 --> 14:16.235
They probably thought you
were just wasting their time.

14:16.270 --> 14:17.636
Maybe you're right. I guess...

14:17.671 --> 14:20.075
guess I could've been a
little more serious about it.

14:20.110 --> 14:21.543
Well, it's not too late.

14:21.578 --> 14:24.282
Maybe you could find a teacher
who could help you learn,

14:24.317 --> 14:26.485
and if you work at it and
get a little better,

14:26.521 --> 14:27.989
they'll see you care about them.

14:28.024 --> 14:29.223
You know what? That's a great idea!

14:29.259 --> 14:30.492
I'll take some lessons.

14:30.528 --> 14:33.197
I'm gonna work really hard
just like my deodorant.

14:33.199 --> 14:35.334
How does a guy like me stay fresh

14:35.370 --> 14:37.405
I use Fat Guys Deodorant.

14:37.440 --> 14:39.208
Whether you're sitting, leaning,

14:39.243 --> 14:42.480
lying down or sitting,
Fat Guys keeps ya dry.

14:42.515 --> 14:45.519
Apply every five minutes, and
you're good for five minutes.

14:45.555 --> 14:48.057
And now for the confusing
commercial backstory.

14:48.092 --> 14:50.367
Ready for the fund-raiser, Dad?

14:50.381 --> 14:51.920
Yeah, be right there, buddy.

14:52.400 --> 14:55.053
We're going to a fund-raiser,
and we share a bedroom.

14:59.580 --> 15:02.282
Mr. Pewterschmidt, you have a visitor.

15:02.318 --> 15:04.018
Hey, buddy, looking good!

15:04.054 --> 15:05.221
So, what are we drinking?

15:05.256 --> 15:07.490
<i>Or better yet, why aren't we drinking?</i>

15:07.526 --> 15:08.961
Get the hell out of here!

15:08.996 --> 15:10.430
I told you I'm done with you!

15:10.465 --> 15:13.301
And besides, I'm off to
the spa down at the club.

15:13.337 --> 15:15.338
How's the temp? Good and hot?

15:17.043 --> 15:19.044
Oh, yeah, that's the stuff.

15:19.080 --> 15:22.885
Hey, did you also not wash
your ass before getting in?

15:22.921 --> 15:25.707
Yeah, that sign.

15:30.200 --> 15:32.234
- There you go, Mr. Glenn.
- Thanks.

15:32.270 --> 15:34.940
Hey, can I get a couple of
extras of these plastic bags?

15:34.975 --> 15:37.645
Let me just test this out quickly.

15:40.417 --> 15:42.252
Yeah, that works. Okay, now you go.

15:42.288 --> 15:44.403
I have to get back to
teaching violin lesson.

15:51.638 --> 15:53.205
Those scales sound terrible!

15:53.241 --> 15:55.075
You fat and lazy! You leave now!

15:55.110 --> 15:56.778
No, please! I got to get better

15:56.813 --> 15:58.531
so I can be as good as my friends.

15:58.736 --> 16:00.171
I really let 'em down.

16:02.624 --> 16:04.023
You fingers no bleeding.

16:04.059 --> 16:05.461
You no try hard enough!

16:05.496 --> 16:07.363
You want me press iron
on your back again?

16:07.398 --> 16:08.800
I'm trying! I'm trying!

16:08.835 --> 16:10.336
Try harder! Play better!

16:15.847 --> 16:18.390
Is somebody making a Cuban sandwich?

16:22.025 --> 16:24.126
Lousy no-good rotten frassum-rassum...

16:26.800 --> 16:28.233
Brian, what's up?

16:28.268 --> 16:30.839
Why are you engaging
in cartoon profanity?

16:30.874 --> 16:32.507
Carter wants nothing to do with me.

16:32.542 --> 16:34.579
- I'm just so mad.
- Don't you mean sad?

16:34.614 --> 16:36.414
You know, about the friendship?

16:36.449 --> 16:38.953
Oh, no, of course, you
mean mad about the money.

16:38.988 --> 16:40.722
All right, fine, it was about the money.

16:40.758 --> 16:42.125
- I miss the money.
- Yes, I know.

16:42.160 --> 16:44.295
I saw all your Instagrams
on his helicopter

16:44.331 --> 16:45.764
like it was your helicopter.

16:45.799 --> 16:47.602
I never said it was my helicopter.

16:47.637 --> 16:49.103
Yeah, never said it wasn't.

16:49.139 --> 16:52.343
The implication was that it was
a regular part of your life.

16:52.378 --> 16:55.416
Anyway, I know this makes me
sound awful, but I almost wish

16:55.451 --> 16:57.885
Carter was still blind
so he'd still need me.

16:57.920 --> 16:59.222
Yeah, but he's not.

17:00.170 --> 17:02.527
<i>But... he could be.</i>

17:02.562 --> 17:05.332
<i>But he isn't. But he should be.</i>

17:05.368 --> 17:06.934
Oh, no.

17:06.969 --> 17:08.438
Come on, it'd be temporary,

17:08.473 --> 17:10.107
just until he realizes I'm a great hang.

17:10.142 --> 17:12.379
But you're not, so I don't
want any part of this.

17:12.414 --> 17:13.747
Okay. I get it. I get it.

17:13.782 --> 17:15.048
Nah, you-you wouldn't want to help me.

17:15.083 --> 17:17.720
What was I thinking? He...
he's your grandfather.

17:17.756 --> 17:20.193
Even though he did say
that thing about you.

17:20.228 --> 17:21.427
What? What did he say about me?

17:21.463 --> 17:23.363
Oh, I... I'm sorry. I
thought I told you.

17:23.399 --> 17:26.470
Um, he said you couldn't cut it
as a member of One Direction.

17:26.505 --> 17:28.674
What?! But they have an opening!

17:28.709 --> 17:29.843
Zayn is gone!

17:29.878 --> 17:31.478
He does know Zayn is gone, right?

17:31.513 --> 17:32.747
Oh, he definitely knows.

17:32.783 --> 17:34.484
Yeah, he-he thinks you
could be in O-Town,

17:34.519 --> 17:35.818
but not One Direction.

17:35.854 --> 17:38.023
Okay, I'm pretty sure
you're manipulating me,

17:38.059 --> 17:40.148
but let's go blind that old bastard.

17:47.909 --> 17:51.580
Listen, Peter, we know you've
been working hard on the violin,

17:51.616 --> 17:54.418
but more importantly, you're our pal,

17:54.455 --> 17:56.188
and we'd like you to
be back in the group.

17:56.223 --> 17:58.727
Really? What if I'm not good enough?

17:58.762 --> 18:00.228
Well, that's the thing.

18:00.264 --> 18:03.401
We decided we'd rather be lousy
with you than great without you.

18:03.436 --> 18:06.240
Joe, no offense, but I'd prefer
to hear it from someone else.

18:06.276 --> 18:08.409
- That's fair.
- So, what do you say, Peter?

18:08.444 --> 18:10.481
Will you come and play
the wedding with us?

18:10.516 --> 18:12.228
Oh, you bet I will! Oh, thanks!

18:12.248 --> 18:14.988
You guys won't regret this,
and don't you worry.

18:15.024 --> 18:18.995
I'll be ready, unlike Lois
getting dressed for a night out.

18:19.031 --> 18:20.598
Tell them the truth!

18:20.633 --> 18:22.000
It's me. It's me.

18:22.036 --> 18:23.871
I'm the one who takes
too long to get ready.

18:23.906 --> 18:25.845
It's 'cause I don't
have any nice clothes.

18:25.847 --> 18:26.627
Peter!

18:26.629 --> 18:28.912
All right. It's 'cause I
don't like the way I look.

18:34.858 --> 18:36.693
Okay, Brian, Carter's in the shower.

18:36.728 --> 18:39.765
As soon as he comes out, we
spray this right in his eyes.

18:39.801 --> 18:41.201
What'd you put in there again?

18:41.236 --> 18:43.706
Oh, it's just tap water
from Flint, Michigan.

18:46.479 --> 18:49.582
♪ And that's how the penis song goes. ♪

18:49.618 --> 18:51.786
Aah! Son of a bitch! My eyes!

18:51.822 --> 18:52.955
You're up.

18:52.991 --> 18:54.257
Carter, what happened?

18:54.293 --> 18:55.593
You look like you could use some help.

18:55.629 --> 18:57.529
Aah! My face! Aah!

18:59.902 --> 19:01.738
Oh, my God!

19:01.773 --> 19:03.907
What did I let money do to me?

19:03.943 --> 19:05.645
Who did this? Who are you?

19:05.680 --> 19:07.748
Carter, it's me, Brian.

19:07.783 --> 19:10.252
I did this, and it's made me realize

19:10.287 --> 19:12.923
that I was blinded by
luxury and comfort,

19:12.959 --> 19:15.663
but now I see that none of
that matters if I don't...

19:15.698 --> 19:17.699
Brian, Brian, hold on.

19:24.513 --> 19:27.950
Looks like we've learned a
lot, and my face is better.

19:38.604 --> 19:40.072
God, I'm so nervous.

19:40.107 --> 19:42.008
You sure you guys want
me to play with you?

19:42.043 --> 19:44.313
Yes, Peter. You play away.

19:44.348 --> 19:45.715
We're a quartet.

19:45.750 --> 19:47.619
Just do the best you can.

19:47.655 --> 19:49.742
You may kiss the bride.

20:13.008 --> 20:14.307
Peter, that was amazing!

20:14.342 --> 20:16.679
I know. Those lessons really paid off!

20:16.714 --> 20:18.514
I'll say! The way you play,

20:18.550 --> 20:20.653
we'll have more gigs than we can handle.

20:20.688 --> 20:23.924
Not a chance. Mr. Washy Washy
took all the joy out of this.

20:23.959 --> 20:26.229
I hate the violin. I hate music.

20:26.264 --> 20:28.464
I hate life, and I'm
never doing this again!

20:29.804 --> 20:32.371
All right, guys, let's go
drink a bunch of free booze

20:32.407 --> 20:34.910
and be a huge presence
in the wedding photos.

20:34.911 --> 21:35.958
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru